{"ts":"2026-07-14T10:06:34.692Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"installable-service-artifact-owner","reportDir":"test-output/reports/installable-service-artifact-owner","consecutive":3,"metric":"priority"}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"installable-service-artifact-owner","reportDir":"test-output/reports/installable-service-artifact-owner","metric":"priority"}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"Given a normalized external manifest, one installable artifact owner resolves remote OCI descriptor bytes or an OCI image-layout descriptor through the same verification path, recomputes the declared sha256 digest, verifies the declared container or WASM payload media type, and enforces an explicit detached-signature policy with typed fail-closed outcomes, without persisting catalog state or activating a runtime.","class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"sealed-owner-scope","statement":"The owner is src/service/installable-service-artifact-resolver.js, exported through src/service/index.js and proved by test/service/installable-service-artifact-resolver.test.js via scripts/checks/run-installable-service-artifact-owner-scenarios.js; architecture/lagrange-service-registry.md may document the executable boundary. No other production owner is in scope."},{"id":"one-verification-path","statement":"Remote OCI providers and local OCI image layouts may differ only in descriptor acquisition. Both must feed the same bounded descriptor digest, OCI-manifest shape, payload-media, and signature-policy verification path."},{"id":"signature-policy","statement":"Signature handling has no implicit default: required, verify_if_present, and disabled are explicit modes. Required and present signatures use detached Ed25519 verification over the canonical sha256 digest against configured trusted public keys; missing, malformed, invalid, or untrusted required evidence fails closed."},{"id":"negative-attacks","statement":"The scenario must reject unsupported sources, provider failures, invalid OCI layout/index/manifest shapes, absent descriptors, oversized descriptors, digest and descriptor-size mismatches, container/WASM media mismatches, and every signature-policy failure while accepting both runtime media types through remote and local sources."},{"id":"downstream-exclusions","statement":"This Quest does not implement registry authentication or wire protocol, build a local layout, persist packages or installations, submit lifecycle mutations, pull container layers into an engine, load WASM bytes, or activate runtimes."},{"id":"red-on-revert-engagement","statement":"Independent verification must show the scenario turns red when digest comparison, runtime/media pairing, or required-signature enforcement is bypassed, and must verify exact-patch plus aggregate fingerprints before checkpoint and handoff."}],"frontierIds":["installable-service-artifact-owner-main"]}}
